rains:
This makes the morn, and this the eve rejoice;
This bids the fost'ring rains and dews descend
To nourish all, to serve one gen'ral end,

rainy:
To-day is not enough or yesterday: God sees it all--
Your length on sunny lawns, the wakeful rainy nights--; tell me--;
(how vain to ask),

raindrop:
Without loving it much,
The raindrop try with my lips,
The grass with my touch;

rainbow:
From playhouse, cabaret and inn
The rainbow lights of Broadway blaze
All gay without, all glad within;

raindrops:
Oh, ever the wind rides by
And ever the raindrops grieve;
But a voice like a woman's sigh

raiment:
Like changing fires on sunset seas;
Her raiment is like morning mist,
Shot opal, gold and amethyst.

Had called me from the house of Life, I know.
So fair their raiment shone I looked in shame
On the unlovely garb in which I came;

rain's:
Whispering to me I could hear;
I felt the rain's cool finger-tips
Brushed tenderly across my lips,

Dah 's a quiet in yo' cabin,
Only fu' de rain's sof soun';
So you 's mighty blessed happy

raih:
I won' care a smidgeon fu' de weathah's frown;
Let de rain go splashin', let de thundah raih,
Dey 's a happy sheltah, an' I 's goin' daih.

